div.p:
When Archilochus the poet came to Lacedaemon, they drove him out that very hour, because they learned that he had written in his poetry that it is better to throw away one's arms than to die.
Some Saian delights in my shield, which beside a bush,Bergk. 2 p. 384 a blameless weapon, ἐντος Brenckius: ἐντὸς I left behind unwillingly;
but I myself escaped the end of death. αὐτὸς - τέλος add Sextus Emp. Hypot. 3 p. 182 That shield, let it go; I shall get another again, no worse.
